1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,390
Hi guys.

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:09,010
It's time to talk about hiring process and learn when and how to use present perfect tense.

3
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,000
I have sent my CV.

4
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:13,010
Good.

5
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:13,640
Okay.

6
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:15,350
Hiring process.

7
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:20,660
So you have created an attractive and professional LinkedIn profile.

8
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:22,970
You have written a top notch CV.

9
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:26,360
Now it's time to look for a job.

10
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:29,390
Where can you find a job?

11
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:34,190
You can check job sites like Indeed or Glassdoor.

12
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:40,370
You can check LinkedIn, Facebook and social medias for some job posts.

13
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:46,640
If there is a company you really want to work at, you can check their website.

14
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:54,110
Usually companies post jobs in career section, or you can ask your friends.

15
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:57,650
Maybe they know about a suitable job for you.

16
00:00:57,650 --> 00:00:59,720
That is called networking.

17
00:01:00,990 --> 00:01:06,630
All right, So let's have a look at examples of job descriptions.

18
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:15,810
So this is a description and company describes their perfect candidate as must be pursuing a bachelor,

19
00:01:15,810 --> 00:01:25,140
master's or PhD degree available for a 12 week internship, strong interpersonal and relationship management

20
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:29,820
skills and ability to adapt in a fast paced environment.

21
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:37,860
So this company is looking for a student in computer science for a three month internship.

22
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:44,490
This person should be a team player and adaptable to different situations.

23
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:53,580
Okay, this job description and company is looking for someone with three plus years of manual testing

24
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:59,430
with experience with Postman Jira Git Jenkins.

25
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:07,330
Someone who has strong analytical and communication skills, problem solving skills and good English

26
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:07,780
levels.

27
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:13,900
So here in a job description, we can see both hard and soft skills.

28
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:23,080
Companies often use phrases like we need someone with hands on experience with web and back end testing.

29
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:27,430
Hands on means practical, real experience.

30
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,370
All right.

31
00:02:29,370 --> 00:02:32,340
So next job description.

32
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:39,500
This company is looking for someone with more than five years of experience in software testing, with

33
00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:48,990
degree in computer science, experience with React and AWS, and someone who really interested in front

34
00:02:48,990 --> 00:02:55,920
end development and who reacts positively to feedback and freely gives feedback.

35
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:04,290
So we can sum up that this company needs a middle to senior frontend developer with technical education

36
00:03:04,290 --> 00:03:09,090
and someone who is a good feedback giver and receiver.

37
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,380
Right?

38
00:03:11,490 --> 00:03:14,690
Okay, so general hiring steps.

39
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:23,250
You have your CV, you find a job description that fits your requirements and skills, so you apply

40
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:24,060
for a job.

41
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:26,730
You send your CV to this company.

42
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:33,270
If your CV looks good for the recruiter, you get an invitation to the interview.

43
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:41,900
But if your CV doesn't match the required position, you get a rejection.

44
00:03:41,910 --> 00:03:42,690
Okay.

45
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:46,740
There are usually from 1 to 5 interviews.

46
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:50,970
It depends on the role and position and company, of course.

47
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:57,480
So if your interviews are good, you might receive an offer from a company.

48
00:03:57,480 --> 00:04:04,800
An offer is a document saying that the company would like to invite you to work for them.

49
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:12,850
If you decide to accept an offer, you start onboarding and working in this company.

50
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:21,970
Okay, There are so many different types of interviews, but let's have a look at the most popular types.

51
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:30,990
So phone screening, it's an interview when recruiter calls you and speaks with you over the phone for

52
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:39,100
five ten minutes and you speak about this position, requirements and expectations, then you might

53
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:41,830
have a culture fit interview.

54
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:51,850
This is an interview with an HR or manager in a company and the company sees if your soft and hard skills

55
00:04:51,850 --> 00:04:55,810
match their requirements and company culture.

56
00:04:55,990 --> 00:05:03,790
If you are applying for a technical position like a developer, okay, you will have a technical interview

57
00:05:03,790 --> 00:05:05,290
or tech call.

58
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:13,120
Usually the last interview before hiring is interview with senior management or the client.

59
00:05:13,630 --> 00:05:21,610
Often when you are applying for a technical position, you will get a task task, for example, to do

60
00:05:21,610 --> 00:05:28,210
some task, to write some code or to create a small application.

61
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,090
All right.

62
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:33,090
Meet my friend Mary.

63
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:39,810
Hi, I'm Mary, a QA engineer with four years of experience.

64
00:05:40,050 --> 00:05:48,390
I have worked at Iglobe company since 2020, but at the moment I am looking for a new role.

65
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:54,750
I want a new challenge and I would be glad to have some automation in my new place.

66
00:05:55,080 --> 00:06:00,210
Last week I found this job opening at the company.

67
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:05,820
I have sent my CV, but I still have not received any feedback.

68
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:09,600
I hope they will invite me to the interview.

69
00:06:09,630 --> 00:06:14,790
I have also applied for two more jobs, so wish me good luck.

70
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,470
Good luck, Mary.

71
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:21,930
Okay, let's have a closer look at some sentences from this text.

72
00:06:22,770 --> 00:06:24,720
I have sent my CV.

73
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:28,930
I still have not received any feedback.

74
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:33,220
I have also applied for two more jobs.

75
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:38,950
Here we used present Perfect to talk about the result.

76
00:06:39,930 --> 00:06:44,760
So I have sent my CV, Mary has sent her CV.

77
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:48,440
I still have not received any feedback.

78
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:51,990
She still has not received any feedback.

79
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:55,350
I have also applied for two more jobs.

80
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:59,430
She has also applied for two more jobs.

81
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:01,550
Okay.

82
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:05,850
Also, we use Present Perfect to talk about our experience.

83
00:07:05,850 --> 00:07:11,490
For instance, I have worked at Iglobe Company since 2020.

84
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,890
Have you worked with Python?

85
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,570
Yes, I have.

86
00:07:15,750 --> 00:07:18,360
So how do we make a present?

87
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,050
Perfect.

88
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:23,580
We take a subject, I or you or she.

89
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:35,310
We add the verb have or has, and then we put the main verb into past participle.

90
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:38,790
For regular verbs, it's just verb.

91
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:48,310
With ed worked, but for irregular, you have to check the third column of irregular verbs table.

92
00:07:48,670 --> 00:07:49,480
Good.

93
00:07:50,430 --> 00:07:57,040
Time for practice, you will find more exercise and more examples in your file.

94
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:58,680
Thank you and bye.
